1. ONE CALCULATION, SEVERAL NAMES
   Five test scores: 72, 85, 90, 64, 79
     add them up           72 + 85 + 90 + 64 + 79 = 390
     divide by how many    390 / 5 = 78
   The same five scores, handed to software under its own names:
     Python  statistics.mean(scores)        78
     SQL     SELECT AVG(score) FROM scores  78.0
   Average, mean, arithmetic mean, arithmetic average, x-bar:
   on these scores every one of them is this calculation, and gives 78.
   Nobody scored 78. The mean is calculated, not picked from the list.

2. WHAT THE ARITHMETIC MEAN KEEPS: THE SUM
   Give every student 78 instead of their own score:
     78 + 78 + 78 + 78 + 78 = 390          the total is still 390
   That is what the mean is: the one number that can stand in for every
   value without changing the total. So the distances from it cancel:
     72 - 78 =  -6
     85 - 78 =  +7
     90 - 78 = +12
     64 - 78 = -14
     79 - 78 =  +1
     sum of the distances = 0              above and below balance exactly
   That balance is the "central" in "central value".

3. WHY "ARITHMETIC": GROWTH KEEPS THE PRODUCT
   Invest 1,000.00. Year 1: +100%. Year 2: -50%.
     1,000.00 -> 2,000.00 -> 1,000.00      back where it started
   Arithmetic mean of the two returns: +25% a year
     1,000.00 x 1.25 x 1.25 = 1,562.50     WRONG: the account holds 1,000.00
   Growth multiplies, so the mean has to keep the PRODUCT of the factors:
     geometric mean of x2 and x1/2 = square root of (2 x 1/2) = 1
     a factor of 1 is +0% a year
     1,000.00 x 1 x 1 = 1,000.00           right

4. WHY "ARITHMETIC": SPEED KEEPS THE TIME
   Drive 60 km at 30 km/h, and the 60 km back at 60 km/h.
     60/30 + 60/60 = 2 + 1 = 3 hours for 120 km
     120 km in 3 hours is 40 km/h
   Arithmetic mean of the speeds: (30 + 60) / 2 = 45 km/h
     at 45 km/h, 120 km takes 2 h 40 min   WRONG: it took 3 h
   Time is distance / speed, so the mean has to keep the sum of 1/speed:
     harmonic mean = 2 / (1/30 + 1/60) = 40 km/h
     at 40 km/h, 120 km takes 3 h          right

5. "AVERAGE" IS A WIDER WORD THAN "MEAN"
   Ten salaries at a small firm; the last one is the owner's:
      32,000   34,000   34,000   34,000   36,000
      38,000   40,000   42,000   45,000  400,000
   Three numbers, each of them honestly called "the average salary":
     mean      73,500    the payroll shared out equally
     median    37,000    the middle: half earn less, half earn more
     mode      34,000    the salary the most people are paid
   9 of the 10 earn less than the mean. "Average" alone did not say which.
